# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local: it is gitignored.
#
# The app runs without any of this. With no database configured it uses the
# in-memory demo data in src/lib/data, which is what every fresh clone and the
# whole test suite do.

# Supabase.
#
# Both values are on the project's API settings page. VITE_SUPABASE_URL is the
# project URL; VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the anon, or publishable, key.
#
# Only the anon key belongs here. It is designed to sit in a browser and is
# protected by row level security, which is why every table has RLS enabled from
# the migration that creates it.
#
# The service role key bypasses RLS entirely. It must never appear in a VITE_
# variable: everything with that prefix is compiled into the JavaScript bundle
# and served to the public. src/lib/supabase.ts refuses to start if it sees one.

# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# SAGIS, the Savannah Area Geographic Information System.
#
# There is no key and no secret here: the service is public and its CORS headers
# reflect the request origin, so the browser calls it directly. See
# docs/SAGIS-API.md.
#
# Left off by default so the demo runs with no network and the test suite stays
# deterministic. Set it to true to read live parcel data and use the county's
# address locator.

# VITE_SAGIS_LIVE=true

# Only needed if the county replatforms its GIS and the path changes.
# VITE_SAGIS_BASE_URL=https://pub.sagis.org/arcgis/rest/services
